<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIA INTERNAL CREDIT RISES 5.36 PCT IN WEEK.</title>
<headline>BULGARIA INTERNAL CREDIT RISES 5.36 PCT IN WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian banks' internal credit</p>
<p>rose to 1,226 billion levs on October 25 from 1,163.6 billion</p>
<p>levs on October 18, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Credit to government rose by 3.32 percent to 501.4 billion</p>
<p>levs, credit to state firms increased 6.95 percent to 327.8</p>
<p>billion levs and lev-denominated credit to private firms picked</p>
<p>up 4.09 percent to 132.3 billion levs.</p>
<p> PERCENTAGE CHANGE	  OCT25-OCT18 OCT25-SEPT27 SEPT27-AUG30</p>
<p> Total internal credit	 +5.36	 +0.50	 +6.57</p>
<p> Credit to govt		  +3.32	 +1.09	 +4.75</p>
<p> Credit to state firms	 +6.95	 +1.05	 +7.39</p>
<p> Lev credit to private firms +4.09	 -1.27	 +1.30</p>
<p> NOMINAL (BILLION LEVS)	  OCT 25    OCT 18    SEPT 27</p>
<p> Total internal credit	  1,226.0   1,163.6    1,213.9</p>
<p> Credit to govt		     501.4     448.3	496.0</p>
<p> Credit to state firms	    327.8     306.5	324.4</p>
<p> Lev credit to private firms    132.3     127.1	134.0</p>
<p> Dlr credit to private firms	1.11	1.12	 1.13</p>
<p>(USD billion)</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-84561</p>
</text>
